prompt.text:
Implement a new TypeScript function that annotates keyed values with membership weights.

Export these declarations:

```typescript
export interface KeyedValue<T> {
    key: string;
    value: T;
}

export interface WeightedValue<T> extends KeyedValue<T> {
    weight: number;
}

export function assignMembershipWeights<T>(
    items: readonly KeyedValue<T>[],
    activeKeys: readonly string[],
    activeWeight?: number,
    inactiveWeight?: number
): WeightedValue<T>[];
```

The default weights are `1` and `0.25`, respectively. Both weights must be finite numbers in the inclusive range `[0, 1]`; otherwise throw `RangeError`. Every item key and active key must be a string containing at least one non-whitespace character; otherwise throw `TypeError`. Membership uses exact, case-sensitive string equality. Duplicate item keys are allowed and are weighted independently. Duplicate active keys have no additional effect. Preserve item order. Return a new array containing new wrapper objects, while preserving each `value` reference as-is. Do not mutate either input array or any input item. Empty arrays are valid.

